Wow, Mr. Poizat, you make a wonderful painting

144
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,980
And I know just what to call it, too

145
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:07,920
Yes, the drowning captain

146
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:09,600
What'd you think?

147
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:11,900
No way! What kind of magic is that?

148
00:09:15,020 --> 00:09:17,980
Honestly, Ryl, you and your half-baked nonsense

149
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:20,700
Yeah, well, somebody had to do something

150
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:23,100
Or else you'd destroy this entire building

151
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:27,360
His magic makes all spells pass through him, but not physical objects

152
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:30,680
Therefore, we need only attack with non-magical items

153
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:35,580
If this building must fall to bring him down, commoners can easily rebuild it

154
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:39,620
I missed the chance to fight a fellow captain in real combat

155
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:44,560
It would've been fun, too, slicing up that ham into tiny little pieces

156
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:49,560
Magic knight captains can't stand around twiddling their thumbs while there's a traitor waiting to be caught

157
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:51,960
At least gotta strike a pose or something

158
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:55,420
Seriously, are you still snoozing?

159
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:59,620
Although you did manage to keep up with us, so I guess you're pretty sharp for being asleep

160
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:02,960
What a pitiful excuse for a man

161
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,860
Running like a coward

162
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:07,980
He was a failure as a captain long before this

163
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:11,520
Why is Yami paying so much attention to Dorothy?

164
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:13,740
Is she the type of woman he likes?

165
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:15,460
Enough

166
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:17,460
Let's leave it there for now

167
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:19,120
Consider this

168
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:21,760
Someone else may be controlling him with magic

169
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:25,800
Well, I'm glad the rest of you were here to help wrangle our traitor

170
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:29,380
I'm afraid I couldn't have gone so easy on him

171
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:31,620
These people are crazy!

172
00:10:32,060 --> 00:10:33,820
And they're the best of the magic knights

173
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:35,880
The best mages in the entire kingdom?

174
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:39,180
Hey, I don't know what you just did, but it was amazing

175
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:41,460
How'd you know where Captain Poizot was?

176
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:43,620
And how'd you break his transparency spell?

177
00:10:43,880 --> 00:10:46,180
Um, well, I just...

178
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:48,940
Never mind, I'm real and I'm 19, who are you?

179
00:10:49,300 --> 00:10:50,640
I'm Asta and I'm 15

180
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:53,260
I can't believe you're only 19 years old and you're a captain

181
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:56,220
Ah, so you're younger than me then

182
00:10:56,220 --> 00:10:58,360
I think we should be friends, what do you say?

183
00:10:58,600 --> 00:10:59,720
Friends? With a captain?

184
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:00,620
Seriously?

185
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,060
Okay, great!

186
00:11:02,380 --> 00:11:03,440
Yay! Awesome!

187
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:06,100
You know, these guys, they're older and

188
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:08,680
I mean, talking to them, it's tough, so

189
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:09,300
Right?

190
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:09,860
Yeah!

191
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:11,900
Boring!

192
00:11:12,620 --> 00:11:12,980
Man!

193
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:14,980
We know we can hear you right

194
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:16,820
And who the hell are you?

195
00:11:17,020 --> 00:11:18,360
Call anyone boring

196
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:21,380
All right

197
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:23,840
So far, all you've done is make excuses

198
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:25,520
Let's hear the truth

199
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:33,440
Now, Gelder

200
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:37,100
Have the answers you've given us up to this point all been truthful?

201
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:38,900
They have

202
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:42,860
You know, I have to hand it to you, Hammy

203
00:11:42,860 --> 00:11:44,440
That's quite an impressive list

204
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,580
Let's see here

205
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:47,180
Beating up your own squad members

206
00:11:47,180 --> 00:11:48,860
Misappropriating magic tools

207
00:11:48,860 --> 00:11:50,900
And smuggling dangerous magic drugs

208
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:54,020
You were way dirty before the whole traitor thing

209
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:57,840
Now, with all that dirt, you're more of a black bull than anyone in my squad

210
00:11:57,840 --> 00:12:01,280
Well, in your case, I guess blackened ham would be more accurate

211
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:01,900
Can't

212
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:04,180
Do you ever stop running your mouth, Yami?

213
00:12:04,820 --> 00:12:07,980
No wonder he didn't want us reading his mind with Marx's spell

214
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:10,620
You didn't mention his worst crime

215
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:12,360
Abducting a guardian mage

216
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:15,840
That's direct cooperation with the Eye of the Midnight Sun

217
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:19,400
At least now we know how they were able to invade the royal capital

218
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:23,420
The fool was so blinded by the offer of rare magic tools

219
00:12:23,420 --> 00:12:25,060
He made a deal with terrorists

220
00:12:25,060 --> 00:12:28,880
So he's greedy and immoral

221
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,860
Does that really surprise anybody?

222
00:12:31,540 --> 00:12:34,740
The Eye of the Midnight Sun likely killed the abducted guardian mage

223
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:36,520
Shortly after the attack on the capital

224
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:40,320
His actions are both unprecedented and unforgivable

225
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:41,940
He was a magic knight

226
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:44,000
Charged with protecting our people

227
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,800
Yet he sold them out instead

228
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:48,800
If word of this got out, the populace might panic

229
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:51,060
So we won't be making this matter public

230
00:12:51,060 --> 00:12:53,680
I want you to take a good look at your squads

231
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:56,160
Make sure none of them have ties to the enemy

232
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:58,180
This cannot happen again

233
00:12:58,180 --> 00:12:59,060
Yes, sir

234
00:12:59,060 --> 00:13:05,720
Well

235
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:11,700
I put on quite the performance

236
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:15,400
Nobody can see through my copy transformation magic

237
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:16,560
So

238
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:16,580
So

239
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:19,280
Which person in the room was actually me?

240
00:13:19,660 --> 00:13:23,280
That ought to keep them from being suspicious for a while at least

241
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:32,760
I'm sorry for keeping you two

242
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:34,780
I won't detain you for long

243
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:37,280
It's a terrible feeling

244
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:40,980
To be betrayed by somebody who once fought alongside you

245
00:13:40,980 --> 00:13:44,980
I sprinted at full speed to get where I am

246
00:13:44,980 --> 00:13:48,240
But as a result I may have made mistakes along the way

247
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:51,780
Did you keep us behind to tell us that?

248
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:55,660
Because if so, Julius, I gotta say you picked the wrong guys

249
00:13:55,660 --> 00:14:00,600
There was one more piece of information the Midnight Sun members revealed during their questioning

250
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,720
Asta?

251
00:14:02,660 --> 00:14:05,500
Remember the hideout they took you to after you were captured?

252
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:08,280
And the mysterious stone tablet that was hidden there?

253
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:10,480
That thing?

254
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:12,360
According to our captives

255
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:15,920
They call the gems embedded in that tablet magic stones

256
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:20,640
They believe that gathering them will allow them to be reborn into their true forms

257
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:22,280
With close ties to the mana

258
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:24,380
Thereby granting them immense power

259
00:14:24,380 --> 00:14:27,380
Apparently that was the reason they targeted Fuegolion

260
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:29,480
Because of the magic stone he wore

261
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:32,980
They think they're gonna be reborn?

262
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:36,280
You sure they haven't been reading too many of those fantasy novels?

